-- title:
--   Zero k-rank for continuous H² at the archimedean place
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, let $S$ be a finite set of rational primes, and let $M$ be a $k$-linear representation of the absolute Galois group $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, realised as $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ acting on a finite-dimensional $k$-vector space. Consider the archimedean member $\mathrm{Sum.inl}\ ()$ of the index type $\mathrm{Unit} \oplus S$ attached to $S$: its local group is the subgroup `archimedeanDecomposition` of the absolute Galois group, and `extArithLoc S (Sum.inl ())` is the inclusion `archimedeanLoc` of that subgroup into the absolute Galois group. Assume that the first group cohomology $H^1$ of the restriction of $M$ along this inclusion is a subsingleton, that is, trivial. The conclusion is that the $k$-rank (`Module.finrank`) of `continuousH2` for this inclusion and this restricted representation is $0$, where `continuousH2 r N` is by definition the quotient of the submodule `levelCocycles₂ r N` by the part of `levelCoboundaries₂ r N` lying inside it. The assertion is thus in rank form rather than an assertion of triviality of that quotient.
--
--   This is the archimedean local contribution to a Greenberg–Wiles style Euler characteristic count: for the decomposition group generated by complex conjugation the second cohomology has the same dimension as the first, so the vanishing of $H^1$ forces the local $H^2$ term to contribute nothing. It is used in [`groupCohomology.greenbergWiles_eq_unramifiedMenu_extArithLoc`](thm.html#groupCohomology.greenbergWiles_eq_unramifiedMenu_extArithLoc), where the local terms of the Greenberg–Wiles formula are matched with the unramified deformation conditions.
-- source:
